We're constantly trying to hold on to the specific, isolated contents of our lives as if capturing those frozen, localized moments is the only way to define who we are or, you know, what is actually happening around us.

01:03.220 --> 01:18.440
Right. And you just get exhausted. But, and this is a big, but what if that entire way of seeing the world, that total obsession with step-by-step, sequential, localized data, what if that is actually an illusion?

