So to fix this crisis, the book argues that we need a completely new kind of math, a math that doesn't just care about the static destinations A and B, but actively cares about the journey between them.

17:40.820 --> 17:45.920
And this brings us to a concept called homotopy type theory, or hot TT.

17:46.420 --> 17:47.640
H-O-T-T, yes.

